{"company":{"ticker":"EOG","name":"EOG Resources","sector":"Energy","industry":"E&P","size":"large","cik":821189},"scores":{"growth":74.0,"quality":78.0,"value":75.0,"acceleration":79.0,"price_momentum":57.0,"reality":77.0,"pricing":44.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"EOG","opportunity_score":67.0,"components":{"structural_trend":49.0,"capital_flow":56.0,"acceleration":79.0,"quality":78.0,"valuation":75.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":69.0,"narrative":75.0,"pricing":48.0,"expectations_gap":21.0,"macro_fit":59.0,"sector_rotation":8.0,"theme_pricing":56.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth +19.1% vs +2.8% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +26.3%, FCF margin +47.3%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":false,"evidence":"ROIC +22.1%, incremental ROIC +19.1%"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +32.9% (+84 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":false,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 49.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":false,"evidence":"Energy rotation score +8"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":false,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 38.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":true,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 75.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA 0.2"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -3.5% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"EOG Resources (EOG) screens at opportunity 67.0 with an expectations gap of 21.0. Reality 69.0 reflects +19.1% TTM revenue growth, +32.9% operating margin and +22.1% ROIC; pricing 48.0 reflects a fair multiple and neutral price momentum. Primary theme exposure: LNG & Energy Security (trend 49.0). Macro fit for Energy in a Goldilocks regime is 59.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["EV/Sales 2.9x (63.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 11x (83.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 17.2%","PEG 0.4","12m return +23%, -8% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (69.0) is running ahead of what is priced (48.0): an expectations gap of +21 pts.","Revenue growth is accelerating (+19.1% TTM, +16.3 pts) while the multiple has not re-rated."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-08-04)","Continued rotation into Energy"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 13% (currently 19.1%)","ROIC falls below 17% (currently 22.1%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 32.9%)","Energy rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +8)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","LNG & Energy Security theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.1335,"current":0.1907},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.1655,"current":0.2207},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.00844187478516173},{"id":"rotation","label":"Energy rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":8.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.599999999999994},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":8.3},{"id":"theme","label":"LNG & Energy Security theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"lng-energy-security","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":49.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"lng-energy-security","theme":"LNG & Energy Security","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"EOG is a best-in-class E&P balance sheet (net debt/EBITDA 0.2x, 33x interest coverage, 3.5% share count shrinkage) generating 33% operating margins and 22% ROIC, trading at 5.6x EV/EBITDA \u2014 cheap against sector peers (sector-relative value 75/100) but NOT cheap against its own history (P/E at the 83rd percentile, EV/EBITDA at the 77th). The screen's +21pt expectations gap is partly an artifact: the reported $580M capex against $13.4B operating cash flow is implausible for an E&P of this size and almost certainly understates full-year development spend, meaning the 17.2% FCF yield and 5.8x P/FCF are flattering. Equally, the +19.1% revenue acceleration from +2.8% is more likely acquisition-aided (Utica/Encino-type consolidation) than a step-change in organic well productivity, so the durability of the acceleration is unproven. The honest case is narrower but still real: a low-leverage, high-ROIC operator buying back ~3.9% of its float annually, priced at a discount to the sector in a commodity tape the market has given up on (Energy rotation +8 vs Technology +73). This is a cash-return and optionality holding on gas/LNG tightness, not a multiple re-rating story.","fundamental_read":"Growth, margins and returns are all moving the right way: revenue +19.1% TTM (from +2.8%), operating margin +84bps to 32.9%, EPS +24.7%, ROIC 22.1% with incremental ROIC 19.1% \u2014 the one flag being that incremental returns sit below the base, implying the marginal dollar of capital (likely acquisition-related) earns less than the installed base. The balance sheet is effectively unlevered (net debt $3.0B on $13.8B EBITDA) and SBC is a trivial 0.85% of revenue, so capital returns are funded, not financed. The $12.8B FCF figure should be treated as unreliable given only $580M of reported capex; normalizing to a mid-cycle E&P reinvestment rate would put FCF yield closer to high-single digits than 17%. Dividend yield is recorded as null, which understates true shareholder yield above the 3.9% buyback figure.","technical_read":"Long-term trend intact \u2014 price 141.84 sits 8.3% above a rising 200-day (130.93) with the 50-day above the 200-day \u2014 but the short-term structure is corrective: price is below both the 20-day (145.65) and 50-day (144.46), RSI 44.6 is neutral-soft and MACD histogram is negative (-0.99). -5.6% over 1m and -7.7% from the 52-week high against +22.9% over 12m describes a consolidation within an uptrend, not a breakdown. The 130-133 zone (200-day) is the level that matters; a clean close below it with negative relative strength would invalidate the trend leg.","market_expectation":"The market is paying roughly 11x earnings and 5.6x EV/EBITDA \u2014 both at the upper end of EOG's own five-year range \u2014 which says the market is NOT pricing stagnation; it is pricing a normal mid-cycle oil strip with modest confidence that capital discipline persists. The flat regime distribution (Goldilocks 26.3 / Reflation 25.1 / Stagflation 23.7 / Contraction 24.9) means macro offers no directional edge, and Energy rotation at +8 says capital is neither fleeing nor arriving. In short: the market expects steady, unexciting cash generation with no terminal-value credit for gas/LNG leverage and no penalty for it either.","what_market_misses":["The sector-relative discount (75/100) is doing the work the screen attributes to an absolute expectations gap \u2014 EOG is cheap versus peers, not versus itself, and that is a rotation trade rather than a re-rating trade.","Gas-weighted optionality is likely under-credited: with US LNG export capacity ramping, Henry Hub-linked volumes and EOG's international/LNG-linked marketing arrangements could be worth more than a pure oil-beta multiple implies.","A 3.9% buyback yield executed at ~11x earnings with a 0.2x levered balance sheet compounds per-share value mechanically even in a flat commodity tape; the market tends to underwrite E&P buybacks as cyclical rather than structural.","Incremental ROIC (19.1%) below base ROIC (22.1%) is a quiet warning the screen scores as a miss but the narrative ignores \u2014 consolidation is diluting marginal returns even as headline growth accelerates."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-08-04 filing): capex disclosure will confirm or refute the FCF distortion, and organic-vs-acquired volume split will test the growth acceleration.","Continued or accelerating buyback authorization / special dividend announcement given the 0.2x leverage and cash balance of $4.9B.","Energy sector rotation turning decisively positive from the current +8 \u2014 Energy is already the second-ranked sector in a tape where nine of eleven sectors are deeply negative.","LNG export capacity additions tightening domestic gas balances and lifting realized gas prices.","Reclaiming the 145-146 zone (20/50-day cluster) with MACD crossing positive would confirm the consolidation is complete."],"risks":["Commodity price is the dominant variable and is entirely absent from the evidence set \u2014 a 20% move in crude or gas swamps every operational improvement listed here.","Valuation is at the 83rd percentile of its own P/E history and 77th on EV/EBITDA; multiple compression back toward the 9.3x median is a ~15% headwind independent of earnings.","The $580M capex figure is likely incomplete; if true maintenance capex is materially higher, the FCF yield, P/FCF and the entire valuation component of the score are overstated.","Acquisition-driven revenue growth carries integration, inventory-quality and marginal-return risk \u2014 visible already in incremental ROIC below base ROIC.","Energy rotation at +8 versus Technology at +73 means flows are concentrated elsewhere; cheap can stay cheap for multiple quarters.","Theme exposure to LNG & Energy Security is only 0.30 weight with a trend score of 49 \u2014 the narrative tailwind is weaker than the headline theme suggests."],"thesis_break_conditions":["Reported capex in the next filing implies normalized FCF yield below ~7%, collapsing the valuation case.","TTM revenue growth falls below 13% (currently 19.1%) or is shown to be entirely inorganic with organic volumes flat-to-down.","ROIC falls below 17% or incremental ROIC falls below 12%, signalling that consolidation is destroying marginal returns.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 32.9%.","Buyback pace decelerates materially below the current 3.9% yield, or net debt/EBITDA rises above 1.0x on further M&A.","Price closes >10% below the 200-day (i.e., below ~118) with negative relative strength versus the S&P.","Energy rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs, or Stagflation+Contraction probability exceeds 55%."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Pressure pumping and completions services (frac fleets, wireline) \u2014 EOG's ability to sustain 19% volume growth depends on service capacity it does not own, and service pricing is where operator capital discipline leaks.","Frac sand and proppant logistics providers in the Permian and Utica basins \u2014 sand intensity per lateral foot rises with longer laterals regardless of operator cost control.","Permian and Appalachian gathering, processing and takeaway midstream \u2014 associated gas from oil-directed drilling is a constraint EOG solves by paying someone else for capacity.","LNG liquefaction and export terminal operators \u2014 EOG's gas needs a destination market to realize international pricing, and that infrastructure is a separate P&L.","Produced-water handling and recycling infrastructure \u2014 water disposal capacity is the binding physical constraint on Permian growth and is increasingly a standalone rate-based business.","Natural gas-fired power generation and behind-the-meter power providers \u2014 rising gas demand from data centers is the demand-side mirror of EOG's supply, and the toll is collected at the generator."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue $27.0B, +19.1% growth versus +2.8% prior quarter; operating margin 32.9% (+84bps YoY); ROIC 22.1%; net debt/EBITDA 0.2x; diluted shares -3.5% YoY; $2.87B of buybacks.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E 10.8x sits at the 83rd percentile of EOG's own five-year range and EV/EBITDA 5.6x at the 77th percentile, versus historical medians of 9.3x and 5.3x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price 141.84 is below the 20-day (145.65) and 50-day (144.46) but 8.3% above a rising 200-day; RSI 44.6, MACD histogram -0.99.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market expects mid-cycle commodity pricing with continued capital discipline, and assigns no premium for gas/LNG optionality.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Energy is the second-best-ranked sector at +8 while Technology sits at +73, implying flows remain concentrated in growth rather than resources.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Reported capex of $580M against $13.4B operating cash flow is implausibly low for an E&P of this scale, so the 17.2% FCF yield and 5.8x P/FCF are likely overstated.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The step-change from +2.8% to +19.1% revenue growth is more likely acquisition-driven than organic, supported by incremental ROIC (19.1%) sitting below base ROIC (22.1%).","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The null dividend yield in the data understates true shareholder yield; actual total return to shareholders exceeds the 3.9% buyback figure.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The deterministic draft's claim that EOG is 'priced for stagnation' is contradicted by its own data showing P/E at the 83rd historical percentile.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Structural US gas demand growth from LNG exports and data-center power could re-rate gas-weighted acreage in a way current oil-beta multiples do not capture.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"With a 0.2x levered balance sheet and $4.9B cash, EOG has capacity for a materially larger buyback or special distribution that would mechanically compound per-share value in a flat tape.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.48}},"technical":{"score":75,"passes":6,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":true,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":false,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":false},"ready":true,"stage":"emerging","close":141.84,"sma50":144.46,"sma150":138.29,"sma200":130.93,"sma150_prev4w":133.93,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":39.4,"pct_from_52w_high":-7.7,"rs_6m":-17.9,"rsi14":44.6,"atr20":3.703,"atr_pct":2.61,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-06-30","filed":"2026-08-04","revenue":27026000000.0,"gross_profit":null,"operating_income":8905000000.0,"net_income":6876000000.0,"ebitda":13752000000.0,"ocf":13358000000.0,"capex":580000000.0,"fcf":12778000000.0,"eps":12.86,"shares_diluted":537250000.0,"cash":4907000000.0,"debt":7926000000.0,"net_debt":3019000000.0,"equ